@page
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }
<div class="page-heading legal-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h1>What we keep, and why.</h1><p class="muted">Last updated @Legal.Updated</p></div>
<article class="legal">
    <p>@Legal.OperatorDescription This page explains what S4 OPS stores about you, where it is kept, and how to get a copy or have it deleted. Questions go to <strong>@Legal.Contact</strong>.</p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <dl class="legal-list">
        <dt>Your sign-in identity</dt><dd>The identifier your sign-in provider gives us, your name and email address, and whether the email is verified. We never see your password.</dd>
        <dt>Your profile</dt><dd>Callsign, home base, SimBrief username, units, time zone, profile picture and workspace preference, if you set them.</dd>
        <dt>Your logbook</dt><dd>Flights you import, add or file from the desktop app: flight number, airports, aircraft, times, and landing rate where known.</dd>
        <dt>Airlines</dt><dd>Airlines you create or join, your roles, and what you add to them: schedule, fleet, logo, invitations.</dd>
        <dt>Activity</dt><dd>A record of account and airline actions (for example "role changed" or "route added"), with who did it and when, so airline administrators can see what changed.</dd>
        <dt>Desktop app</dt><dd>The app version you last signed in with and when, so we know which versions are still in use.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>We do not store your IP address, use advertising or tracking cookies, or run analytics. The only cookies are the ones that keep you signed in and protect forms from forgery.</p>
    <p>The desktop app also keeps your flights and settings on your own PC. That copy stays under your control and is not covered by deletion here.</p>

    <h2>Who handles it</h2>
    <dl class="legal-list">
        <dt>Auth0 (Okta)</dt><dd>Sign-in, passwords, passkeys and multi-factor authentication.</dd>
        <dt>Render</dt><dd>Runs the S4 OPS server, in the United States (Ohio).</dd>
        <dt>Neon</dt><dd>Hosts the database.</dd>
        <dt>Cloudflare</dt><dd>Domain and network protection, once the service moves to s4ops.com.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>We don't sell your data or share it with anyone else. Members of an airline you join can see your display name, roles and what you do in that airline.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Get a copy.</strong> <a href="/Account/Profile#your-data">Download your data</a> from your profile at any time: a ZIP with your account, profile, airlines, logbook, activity and profile picture.</li>
        <li><strong>Correct it.</strong> Edit your profile, logbook and airline details directly.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete it.</strong> <a href="/Account/Delete">Delete your account</a> from your profile. Your account locks straight away and is erased after @Legal.DeletionGraceDays days, unless you sign in and cancel. We then delete your profile, logbook, picture and memberships, remove your name and email from the account record, and remove your sign-in from Auth0. Airline history keeps an anonymous "deleted pilot" in your place. If you own an airline, transfer it first.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>For as long as you have an account. After deletion nothing that identifies you remains, apart from backups, which the database host overwrites within a few days.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this page changes in a way that matters, we'll say so on the site before the change takes effect. The date at the top shows the current version.</p>
</article>
